{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Sampling Methods Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Uniform and inverse CDF sampling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import random"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sample_uniform(a, b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return a + (b - a) * random.random()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sample_exponential_inverse_cdf(lam):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    u = random.random()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return -math.log(u) / lam"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Generate 10,000 exponential samples and verify the mean is 1/lambda."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Rejection sampling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def rejection_sample(target_pdf, proposal_sample, proposal_pdf, M):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    while True:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = proposal_sample()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        u = random.random()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if u < target_pdf(x) / (M * proposal_pdf(x)):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Use rejection sampling to draw from a truncated normal distribution. Verify the shape by histogramming the samples."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Importance sampling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def importance_sampling_estimate(f, target_pdf, proposal_pdf, proposal_sample, n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = proposal_sample()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        w = target_pdf(x) / proposal_pdf(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total += f(x) * w"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return total / n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Estimate E[X^2] under a normal distribution using a uniform proposal. Compare to the known answer (mu^2 + sigma^2)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Monte Carlo estimation of pi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def monte_carlo_pi(n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    inside = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(n):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = random.uniform(-1, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        y = random.uniform(-1, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if x*x + y*y <= 1:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            inside += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return 4 * inside / n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Metropolis-Hastings MCMC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def metropolis_hastings(target_log_pdf, proposal_sample, proposal_log_pdf, x0, n_samples, burn_in):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    samples = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = x0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(n_samples + burn_in):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x_new = proposal_sample(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        log_alpha = (target_log_pdf(x_new) + proposal_log_pdf(x, x_new)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                     - target_log_pdf(x) - proposal_log_pdf(x_new, x))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if math.log(random.random()) < log_alpha:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            x = x_new"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if i >= burn_in:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            samples.append(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return samples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Sample from a bimodal distribution (mixture of two Gaussians). Visualize the chain's trajectory."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Gibbs sampling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def gibbs_sampling_2d(conditional_x_given_y, conditional_y_given_x, x0, y0, n_samples, burn_in):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x, y = x0, y0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    samples = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(n_samples + burn_in):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        x = conditional_x_given_y(y)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        y = conditional_y_given_x(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if i >= burn_in:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            samples.append((x, y))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return samples"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 7: Temperature sampling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def softmax(logits):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    max_l = max(logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    exps = [math.exp(z - max_l) for z in logits]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total = sum(exps)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [e / total for e in exps]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def temperature_sample(logits, temperature):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    scaled = [z / temperature for z in logits]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    probs = softmax(scaled)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return sample_from_probs(probs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Show how temperature changes the output distribution for a set of token logits."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 8: Top-k and top-p sampling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def top_k_sample(logits, k):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    indexed = sorted(enumerate(logits), key=lambda x: -x[1])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    top = indexed[:k]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    top_logits = [l for _, l in top]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    probs = softmax(top_logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    idx = sample_from_probs(probs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return top[idx][0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def top_p_sample(logits, p):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    probs = softmax(logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    indexed = sorted(enumerate(probs), key=lambda x: -x[1])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cumsum = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    selected = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for token_idx, prob in indexed:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        cumsum += prob"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        selected.append((token_idx, prob))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if cumsum >= p:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            break"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sel_probs = [pr for _, pr in selected]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total = sum(sel_probs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sel_probs = [pr / total for pr in sel_probs]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    idx = sample_from_probs(sel_probs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return selected[idx][0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 9: Reparameterization trick"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def reparam_sample(mu, sigma):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    epsilon = random.gauss(0, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return mu + sigma * epsilon"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def reparam_gradient(mu, sigma, epsilon):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dz_dmu = 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dz_dsigma = epsilon"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return dz_dmu, dz_dsigma"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Demonstrate that gradients flow through the reparameterized sample but not through direct sampling."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 10: Gumbel-Softmax"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def gumbel_sample():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    u = random.random()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return -math.log(-math.log(u))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def gumbel_softmax(logits, temperature):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    gumbels = [math.log(p) + gumbel_sample() for p in logits]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return softmax([g / temperature for g in gumbels])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Show how decreasing temperature makes the output approach a one-hot vector."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Full implementations with all visualizations are in `code/sampling.py`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Implement inverse CDF sampling for the Cauchy distribution. The CDF is F(x) = 0.5 + arctan(x)/pi. Generate 10,000 samples and plot the histogram against the true PDF. Notice the heavy tails (extreme values far from center).\n\n2. Use rejection sampling to generate samples from a Beta(2, 5) distribution using a Uniform(0, 1) proposal. Plot the accepted samples against the true Beta PDF. What is the theoretical acceptance rate?\n\n3. Estimate the integral of sin(x) from 0 to pi using Monte Carlo with 1,000, 10,000, and 100,000 samples. Compare the error at each level. Verify that the error scales as O(1/sqrt(N)).\n\n4. Implement Metropolis-Hastings to sample from a 2D distribution p(x, y) proportional to exp(-(x^2 * y^2 + x^2 + y^2 - 8*x - 8*y) / 2). Plot the samples and the chain trajectory. Experiment with different proposal standard deviations.\n\n5. Build a complete text generation demo: given a vocabulary of 10 words with logits, generate sequences of 20 tokens using (a) greedy, (b) temperature=0.7, (c) top-k=3, (d) top-p=0.9. Compare the diversity of outputs across 5 runs."
      ]
    }
